"id": "d10-4#0",
"l": "d10-4",
"q": "You quantize a weight group symmetrically to int4 (levels −7…7). Its largest magnitude is 1.4. What is the scale, and what does a weight of 0.08 become?",
"o": [
"Scale 0.1; 0.08 → 0.1",
"Scale 0.2; 0.08 rounds to level 0, so it becomes 0",
"Scale 1.4; 0.08 stays 0.08"
],
"k": 1,
"e": "Scale = max |w| / 7 = 1.4 / 7 = 0.2. Then 0.08 / 0.2 = 0.4, which rounds to 0. Small weights in a group with a large one get wiped out, which is why groups are kept small (64–128 weights) and outliers get special handling."
