"k": 1,
"e": "Scattered zeros are stored in the same dense matrix, so the matmul does the same work. To get speed you need a pattern the hardware or library exploits: removing whole channels/heads (a smaller dense matrix) or the 2:4 pattern that sparse tensor cores skip."
