"e": "<code>.item()</code> needs the actual value on the CPU, so Dynamo must stop the graph, run Python, and start a new graph. Many breaks mean little fusion and extra overhead (and possibly recompiles). Keep compiled regions free of prints, <code>.item()</code> and data-dependent branches."
